  "explanation": {
    "markdown": "## At, in, on: Prepositions of time\n\n![Detailed grammar chart explaining the use of time prepositions 'at', 'in', and 'on' with examples for days, months, seasons, years, and specific times of day.](/uploads/grammar/a1/at-in-on-prepositions-time/img-1.png)\n\n### **At**\n\nUse **at** with times of day, including mealtimes, bedtime, etc.\n\n-   ***at*** *3 o’clock, **at** 10.30 am, **at** noon, **at** dinnertime, **at** bedtime, **at** sunrise, **at** sunset, **at** the moment*\n\nUse **at** in the following common expressions:\n\n-   **at** the weekend: *I don’t usually work **at** the weekend.*\n-   **at** Christmas/Easter: *I stay with my family **at** Christmas.*\n-   **at** the same time**:** *We finished the test **at** the same time.*\n-   **at** present/**at** the moment**:** *He’s not home **at** present. Try later.*\n\n### **In**\n\nUse **in** with [months, seasons](https://test-english.com/vocabulary/a1/days-months-seasons-a1-english-vocabulary/), years, decades, centuries and long periods of time in general.\n\n-   ***in*** *May, **in** the summer, **in** 1990, **in** the 1990s, **in** the 20th century, **in** the Ice Age, **in** the past/future*\n\n### **On**\n\nUse **on** followed by days and dates.\n\n-   ***on*** *Sunday, **on** Tuesday mornings, **on** 6 March, **on** 25 December 2010, **on** Christmas Day, **on** Independence Day, **on** my birthday, **on** New Year’s Eve*\n\n### Parts of the day:\n\n-   **in** the morning\n-   **in** the afternoon\n-   **in** the evening\n-   **at** night\n\n### **Last**, **next**, **every** and **this**\n\nWhen we say **last, next, every, this**, we do not use **at, in, on**.\n\n-   *I went to London **last*** *June*. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/at-in-on-prepositions-time/img-2.png)\n-   *I went to London **in last*** *June*. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/at-in-on-prepositions-time/img-3.png)\n-   *He’s coming back **next*** Tuesday. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/at-in-on-prepositions-time/img-4.png)\n-   *He’s coming back **on next*** Tuesday. ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/at-in-on-prepositions-time/img-5.png)\n-   *I go home **every** Easter.* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/at-in-on-prepositions-time/img-6.png)\n-   *I go home **at every** Easter.* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/at-in-on-prepositions-time/img-7.png)\n-   *We’ll call you **this** evening.* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/at-in-on-prepositions-time/img-8.png)\n-   *We’ll call you **in this** evening.* ![](/uploads/grammar/a1/at-in-on-prepositions-time/img-9.png)",
